### Group POST/GET/$export demo — see docs/fenix_architecture.md,
### cmd/fenix/fhirserver/group.go and export.go
#
# Uses the REAL "sim" test data (test/data/sim/) through the REAL FHIR
# conversion SQL (queries/sim/fhir/*.sql), loaded via the real ETL pipeline
# and wired into the live query compiler by
# config/queries/sources/sim/sim.yaml.
#
# Setup (once):
#   go run ./cmd/fenix -config config/group-demo.yaml -cmd load
#   FENIX_DEIDENT_KEY=ZGVtby1vbmx5LW5vdC1hLXJlYWwtc2VjcmV0 go run ./cmd/fenix -config config/group-demo.yaml -cmd serve -source sim
# (de-identification is enabled in config/group-demo.yaml, so $export below
# proves patient numbers are hashed, never raw, in its output — same demo-only
# key `make deident-pipeline-demo` uses, never a real secret)
#
# Seeded patients:
#   123 — two Observations, both status=final        (test/data/sim/AlgemeneMeting.csv)
#   456 — two Observations, both status=final
#   789 — one Observation,  status=preliminary
# So Observation?status=final is a genuine dynamic SUBSET: 123 and 456 only,
# 789 excluded.

@base = http://127.0.0.1:8080/r4

### Sanity check: every Observation (5 rows: 4 final, 1 preliminary)
GET {{base}}/Observation
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Sanity check: status=final narrows to patients 123 and 456 only
GET {{base}}/Observation?status=final
Accept: application/fhir+json

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Struct-based param fallback (cmd/fenix/fhirserver/paramfilter.go) —
### ?code= isn't configured as SQL pushdown for Observation
### (config/queries/sources/sim/sim.yaml only lists status/patient), so the
### SQL itself returns every row regardless of ?code=. filterUnwiredParams
### catches it afterwards instead: it looks up "code"'s SearchParameter type
### (token) in terminology/searchparameter/search-parameter.json and
### filters the already-converted FHIR structs in Go. Same observations as
### test/data/sim/AlgemeneMeting.csv: 123 has codes MCD_A/MCD_L, 456 has
### MCD_B/LA6751-7, 789 (preliminary) has MCD_P.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Unwired token param alone — only the one observation coded MCD_A (patient 123)
GET {{base}}/Observation?code=MCD_A
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Combine a pushed-down param (status) with an unwired one (code) — only patient 456's MCD_B observation
GET {{base}}/Observation?status=final&code=MCD_B
Accept: application/fhir+json

### FHIR token "system|code" syntax also works — same single match as above
GET {{base}}/Observation?code=https://santeon.nl/sct|MCD_B
Accept: application/fhir+json

### date is also unwired (not in sim.yaml's pushdown list), and maps to the
### choice-type field Observation.effective[x] — filterUnwiredParams resolves
### that to the actual JSON key (effectiveDateTime here) via resolveField's
### prefix fallback (cmd/fenix/fhirserver/paramfilter.go). All 5 seeded
### observations are dated 2023-10-13, so ge2023-10-14 proves the filter is
### real (0 results, not just passed through) while ge2023-10-13 proves it
### isn't over-filtering (all 5 still come back).

### No observation is on/after 2023-10-14 — expect total: 0
GET {{base}}/Observation?date=ge2023-10-14
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Every observation is on/after 2023-10-13 — expect total: 5
GET {{base}}/Observation?date=ge2023-10-13
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Combine with the pushed-down status param — expect total: 4 (the 789/preliminary row drops out)
GET {{base}}/Observation?status=final&date=ge2023-10-13
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Create a Group whose membership is dynamically filtered to status=final — expect 123 and 456, NOT 789
# @name createGroup
POST {{base}}/Group
Content-Type: application/fhir+json
Accept: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Group",
  "type": "person",
  "actual": false,
  "name": "SIM patients with a final Observation",
  "extension": [
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/bulkdata/StructureDefinition/member-filter",
      "valueString": "Observation?status=final"
    }
  ]
}

### GET the group above — membership is resolved fresh on every call
GET {{base}}/Group/{{createGroup.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Unknown group id -> 404 OperationOutcome
GET {{base}}/Group/does-not-exist
Accept: application/fhir+json

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### Bulk $export — one call does everything: resolve membership, fetch
### Patient + Observation, scope to members, de-identify under one shared
### RunID (so a hashed Observation.subject matches the same patient's
### hashed Patient.id), return NDJSON. The caller never sees 123/456/789.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Kick off the export — 202 Accepted + Content-Location header
# @name kickoffExport
POST {{base}}/Group/{{createGroup.response.body.id}}/$export?_type=Patient,Observation
Prefer: respond-async
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Poll status — FENIX computes synchronously, so this is already 200 + manifest
# Copy the job id from kickoffExport's Content-Location response header into the URL below
# (REST Client doesn't expose response headers as {{var.response.headers.X}} the way it does the body)
GET {{base}}/$export-status/1528feea-0eb6-4c5e-bed6-bf136495d5eb
Accept: application/json

### Download the de-identified Patient NDJSON — only hashed ids, never 123/456/789
GET {{base}}/$export-files/1528feea-0eb6-4c5e-bed6-bf136495d5eb
Accept: application/fhir+ndjson

### Download the de-identified Observation NDJSON — subject references match the Patient file's hashed ids
GET {{base}}/$export-files/77e00385-726e-4a53-a615-7bc6f728ea70/Observation.ndjson
Accept: application/fhir+ndjson

### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
### _typeFilter — narrows ONE resource type's export independently of the
### group's own membership. This group's member-filter is just
### "Observation" (no params), so membership is all 3 patients (123, 456,
### 789) regardless of status. _typeFilter=Observation?status=final below
### then narrows ONLY the Observation output to the 4 final rows — Patient
### still exports all 3 members, including 789, even though 789's own
### Observation gets excluded from Observation.ndjson by the typeFilter.
### ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

### Broad group: every patient with any Observation, any status — expect 123, 456, 789
# @name createBroadGroup
POST {{base}}/Group
Content-Type: application/fhir+json
Accept: application/fhir+json

{
  "resourceType": "Group",
  "type": "person",
  "actual": false,
  "name": "All SIM patients with any Observation",
  "extension": [
    {
      "url": "http://hl7.org/fhir/uv/bulkdata/StructureDefinition/member-filter",
      "valueString": "Observation"
    }
  ]
}

### Sanity check: membership really is all 3 patients
GET {{base}}/Group/{{createBroadGroup.response.body.id}}
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Export with _typeFilter — manifest should show Patient count=3, Observation count=4
# @name kickoffFilteredExport
POST {{base}}/Group/{{createBroadGroup.response.body.id}}/$export?_type=Patient,Observation&_typeFilter=Observation%3Fstatus%3Dfinal
Prefer: respond-async
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Poll status — paste the job id from kickoffFilteredExport's Content-Location header
GET {{base}}/$export-status/PASTE_JOB_ID_FROM_CONTENT_LOCATION_HEADER
Accept: application/json

### Patient.ndjson — all 3 patients (typeFilter doesn't touch Patient, no _typeFilter entry was given for it)
GET {{base}}/$export-files/PASTE_JOB_ID_FROM_CONTENT_LOCATION_HEADER/Patient.ndjson
Accept: application/fhir+ndjson

### Observation.ndjson — only the 4 status=final rows; 789's preliminary Observation is excluded here
### even though 789 IS a group member and DOES appear in Patient.ndjson above
GET {{base}}/$export-files/PASTE_JOB_ID_FROM_CONTENT_LOCATION_HEADER/Observation.ndjson
Accept: application/fhir+ndjson

### Malformed _typeFilter (no resource type before '?') -> 400 OperationOutcome
POST {{base}}/Group/{{createBroadGroup.response.body.id}}/$export?_type=Observation&_typeFilter=%3Fstatus%3Dfinal
Prefer: respond-async
Accept: application/fhir+json

### Unknown export job -> 404 OperationOutcome
GET {{base}}/$export-status/does-not-exist
Accept: application/json
